# Copy to .env, which is gitignored, and put real tokens in it.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Generate each token with:
#
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
# Each token is an independent dataset. One token is one person's set of devices; two readers sharing
# a server get one token each and cannot see each other's data. Comma-separated, no spaces needed.
#
# A token is the ONLY credential protecting a dataset — there is no password and no second factor — so
# generate it rather than inventing one. The server refuses anything shorter than 32 characters.
#
# Rotating a token cuts off every device using it. Note that the app derives its encryption key from
# the token as well, so a rotation is a fresh start rather than a new password for the same data. See
# the README.
CMDV_SYNC_TOKENS=replace-me-with-openssl-rand-base64-32

# Alternatively, point at a file with one token per line — which is what Docker secrets mount. Set
# one or the other, never both.
# CMDV_SYNC_TOKENS_FILE=/run/secrets/cmdv_sync_tokens
